# Class-table features are rules text unless an explicit PCGen numeric grant is present.
Wraith Form Rounds (Reference)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DEFINE:SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_ROUNDS|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_ROUNDS|if(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL>=20,0,SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL+SPHERES_CASTING_ABILITY)	DESC:%SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_ROUNDS daily wraith form rounds; zero denotes unlimited only when Form Unlimited is one; apply to qualifying rolls or uses only.
Wraith Form Unlimited (Reference)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DEFINE:SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_UNLIMITED|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_UNLIMITED|if(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL>=20,1,0)	DESC:%SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_UNLIMITED unlimited wraith form at level 20; activation remains required; apply to qualifying rolls or uses only.
Wraith Haunt DC (Reference)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DEFINE:SPHERES_WRAITH_HAUNT_DC|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_HAUNT_DC|10+floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)+SPHERES_CASTING_ABILITY	DESC:%SPHERES_WRAITH_HAUNT_DC save DC for wraith haunts that call for saves; apply to qualifying rolls or uses only.
Wraith Possession DC (Reference)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DEFINE:SPHERES_WRAITH_POSSESSION_DC|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_POSSESSION_DC|if(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL<2,0,10+floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)+SPHERES_CASTING_ABILITY)	DESC:%SPHERES_WRAITH_POSSESSION_DC possession save DC from level 2; host effects are table-resolved; apply to qualifying rolls or uses only.
Wraith Possession Targets (Reference)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DEFINE:SPHERES_WRAITH_POSSESSION_TARGETS|0	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_POSSESSION_TARGETS|if(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL<2,0,if(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL<10,1,max(2,SPHERES_CASTING_ABILITY)))	DESC:%SPHERES_WRAITH_POSSESSION_TARGETS simultaneously possessed creatures; actions are shared, not multiplied; apply to qualifying rolls or uses only.
Wraith Class Features 1	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 1: Casting, haunt path (path sphere), spell pool, wraith form. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 2	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 2: Haunt path (path possession), possession. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 3	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 3: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 4	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 4: Haunt path (path skill). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 5	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 5: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 6	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 6: Possession (extraordinary abilities). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 7	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 7: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 8	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 8: Haunt path (improved path possession). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 9	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 9: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 10	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 10: Greater possession. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 11	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 11: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 12	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 12: Possession (supernatural abilities). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 13	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 13: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 14	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 14: Haunt path (greater path possession). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 15	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 15: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 16	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 16: Possession (spell-like abilities). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 17	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 17: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 18	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 18: Possession (spheres). See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 19	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 19: Wraith haunt. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Class Features 20	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature	DESC:Level 20: Wraith form mastery. See https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/wraith for effects, timing and prerequisites.
Wraith Amnesiac Possession	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:As part of ending a possession, the wraith may force the host creature to succeed on a Will save or forget the duration of the possession as the Amnesia talent of the Mind sphere.
Wraith Benevolent Passenger	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:When possessing an object or a willing creature, the wraith gains the benefits of the Silent Spell and Still Spell metamagic feats. If the wraith already possesses either of these feats, reduce the spell point cost of the possessed feat by 1 [minimum 0].
Wraith Consume Host	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:While possessing a living creature, the wraith may spend a spell point as a move action to deal 1d6 untyped damage per 2 class levels to the host. A successful Fortitude save halves this damage. The wraith heals a number of hit points equal to the damage dealt. A creature that successfully saves against this ability becomes immune to it for the duration of the possession.
Wraith Deep Phase	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:While in wraith form, the wraith may spend a spell point as a move action to attempt to pass through objects thicker than his own space. The wraith may move up to his speed through solid matter. If the wraith does not end his movement in a space he could occupy, he is shunted back to his starting position, taking 1d6 untyped damage per 5 feet traveled.
Wraith Disorienting Possession	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:When the wraith’s active possession ends, he may force the possessed creature to attempt a Fortitude save or be nauseated for a number of rounds equal to the wraith’s casting ability modifier. A successful save reduces this to being sickened for 1 round.
Wraith Dominate Ooze	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith may possess mindless creatures of the ooze type, bypassing the immunity to mind-affecting effects granted by the ooze type.
Wraith Expanded Path Possession (requires haunt path - path sphere of the selected path)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith gains the path possession ability of a path he does not possess. This wraith haunt may be taken more than once, each time another path possession may be selected.
Wraith Expanded Path Possession - Improved (requires expanded path possession - wraith 12)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,12	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Wraith Wraith Haunt,Wraith Expanded Path Possession (requires haunt path - path sphere of the selected path)	DESC:The wraith gains the improved path possession ability of a path he chose for expanded path possession. This wraith haunt may be taken more than once, each time another expanded path possession may be selected.
Wraith Extra Incorporeality	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_FORM_ROUNDS|4|PREVARLT:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,20	DESC:The wraith gains 4 additional rounds of his wraith form ability per day. This talent may be taken more than once; the bonus rounds stack.
Wraith Forced Wraith Form (requires share wraith form)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Wraith Wraith Haunt,Wraith Share Wraith Form	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	PREVARLT:SPHERES_WRAITH_FORCED_FORM_COUNT,2	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_FORCED_FORM_COUNT|1	DESC:The wraith may target an unwilling creature with Share Wraith Form via a melee touch attack. A successful Will save negates this effect. An unwilling creature cannot choose to end this effect, though the wraith may end it normally. The target creature may attempt a new Will save each round as a full-round action to end the effect early. This wraith haunt may be taken a second time to allow the wraith to use this ability with a ranged touch attack with a range of close [25 feet + 5 feet per 2 class levels].
Wraith Ghostly Fade	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:While in wraith form, the wraith may spend a spell point as a free or immediate action to gain concealment until the start of his next turn. At 4th level and every 4 levels thereafter, this concealment persists for an additional round.
Wraith Ghost Glide (requires wraith 7)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,7	DESC:The wraith gains a fly speed equal to his base speed with perfect maneuverability while in wraith form.
Wraith Ghost Glide - Improved (requires wraith 11)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,11	DESC:The fly speed granted by ghost glide applies even when the wraith is not in wraith form, though when not in wraith form the maneuverability decreases to average.
Wraith Ghost in the Machine (requires object ride - Technologist feat)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:While possessing a technological device, the wraith may spend spell points in place of charges. The Technologist feat can be found in the Pathfinder Campaign Setting: Technology Guide book.
Wraith Ghostly Talent	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith gains a talent from his path sphere as a bonus talent. This wraith haunt may be selected more than once; each time the wraith selects an additional talent.
Wraith Hidden Rider	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:While possessing another creature or object, the wraith may hide from the divine ability of the Divination sphere and spells of the Divination school and pass through wards that would affect a possessing creature such as magic circle against evil or the effects of a forbiddance spell. The wraith must attempt a Will save against the spell or sphere ability [even if it does not normally allow a saving throw]. If he succeeds, the spell treats him as if he were his host [for instance, Divine Alignment would reveal only the host’s alignment, and forbiddance keyed to the host’s alignment would not damage the wraith]. If the wraith’s saving throw fails, the spell functions against him as normal.
Wraith Hidden Possessor	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:Creatures that are not aware of the wraith or do not count the wraith as a hostile creature take a -2 penalty on saves against his possession ability.
Wraith Into Thin Air	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith may spend a spell point to activate his wraith form ability as an immediate action. If the wraith possesses the ghostly fade wraith haunt, he may choose to activate it as part of this immediate action, paying the spell point cost for that ability as usual.
Wraith Lengthened Control	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:Upon successfully using his possession ability, the wraith may spend a spell point as a free action to calculate the duration of the possession as if the creature’s CR was 1 tier lower per Table: Possession Duration. For creatures with a challenge rating below the wraith’s class level -4, the duration instead increases from 10 minutes/level to 1 hour per level for active possession or to indefinite [new save granted every 24 hours] for passive possession.
Wraith Lingering Incorporeality	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:When the wraith ends his wraith form ability, he may choose to remain in wraith form for two additional rounds without spending any rounds from his daily allotment. If the wraith was in wraith form when activating his possession ability, he automatically regains his wraith form upon ending the possession if within this time.
Wraith Moan	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:As a standard action, the wraith may emit an unearthly moan, allowing the wraith to attempt an Intimidate check to demoralize all hostile creatures within 30 feet. If using Spheres of Might, the wraith instead may choose to gain the Gladiator sphere or a talent from that sphere if it is already possessed. If using this option, this wraith haunt may be taken more than once, granting an additional talent from the Gladiator sphere each time.
Wraith Object Ride	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith may spend a spell point to passively possess an object for up to 1 hour per level. Attended objects receive a Will save. The object can be no smaller than Tiny and no larger than Huge. At level 10, the minimum object size decreases to Diminutive and the maximum increases to Gargantuan. The wraith retains his normal senses while possessing an object. Additionally, the wraith may designate a single object within the normal limits as his refuge. Passively possessing the refuge does not require a spell point. Designating an object as a refuge requires a 1-hour ritual. Designating a new object causes any previous refuges to cease functioning as a refuge. The wraith may speak in his normal voice while in his refuge object.
Wraith Possess Armaments (requires Enhancement sphere or object ride or path of the poltergeist)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Wraith Wraith Haunt,Wraith Object Ride],[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Wraith Haunt Path,Wraith Path of the Poltergeist]	DESC:When possessing a weapon, shield, or suit of armor, the wraith may automatically grant it the benefit of one enhancement that he possesses for the duration of the possession. The object must be a valid target for the enhancement. The wraith uses his class level as his caster level to determine the effect of this enhancement. This stacks normally with caster levels gained from other sources. Any additional spell point cost of the enhancement must be paid as usual. Should the Animate Object enhancement be used, the wraith may issue commands to the object while possessing it.
Wraith Ranged Possession	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith may attempt to possess valid targets within close range [25 feet + 5 feet per 2 class levels].
Wraith Reactive Possession (requires possess armaments or path of the poltergeist improved path possession)	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	PREMULT:1,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Wraith Wraith Haunt,Wraith Possess Armaments (requires Enhancement sphere or object ride or path of the poltergeist)],[PREMULT:2,[PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Wraith Haunt Path,Wraith Path of the Poltergeist],[PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,8]]	DESC:When the wraith takes damage from a manufactured weapon, he may attempt to possess that weapon as an immediate action, paying the normal spell point cost.
Wraith Share Wraith Form	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith may touch a willing creature as a standard action, granting them the benefits of his wraith form and any wraith haunts that modify it that the wraith possesses [such as lingering incorporeality]. Either the creature or the wraith may end this effect as a free action. The touched creature expends rounds of wraith form from the wraith’s pool. The wraith may end this effect as a free action.
Wraith Steal Thoughts	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith is intuitively aware of what actions are against his host’s nature. When possessing a creature, the wraith may spend a spell point as a standard action to read its mind, allowing him to attempt a single Knowledge check using its skill modifiers [even if the wraith has previously failed the same check using his own modifiers] or receive the answer to a single question that the creature would know [such as ‘Where did I leave my key?’ or ‘What is my mother’s maiden name?’]. A successful Will save negates this effect. A creature is aware of succeeding on this save, sensing the mental probing of the wraith, though not the details of the information sought. Additional uses of this ability while possessing the same creature do not allow Knowledge checks to be retried if they would not otherwise be possible to retry.
Wraith Wraith’s Blade	CATEGORY:Wraith Wraith Haunt	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,3	DESC:The wraith may spend a spell point as a swift action to cause all his attacks to become incorporeal touch attacks [and thus be resolved as touch attacks, though effects that apply against incorporeal touch attacks function normally] until the end of his turn. This ability also allows the attacks to be made against corporeal targets while wraith form is active.
Wraith Haunts	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpheresClassFeature.SpheresWraithHaunt	DESC:Wraith haunt selections; each haunt retains its own prerequisites.
Wraith Path of the Ancestor	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Protection Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_PROTECTION|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Knowledge (History)	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (History)|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Rather than a malevolent controller, an ancestor protects those he is attached to. Path Sphere: Protection Path Possession: When a willing creature the ancestor is possessing takes hit point damage, as a free action that can be taken even when it is not his turn, the ancestor may choose to redirect up to half the damage to himself. The damage is determined after the possessed creature’s damage reduction, immunity, resistance, and vulnerability have been calculated and may not be further reduced or redirected by any means. Additionally, the ancestor may choose to count the possessed willing creature as himself for the purposes of effects that only target self. Path Skill: Knowledge [history] [Int]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Anima - Nature	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Nature Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_NATURE|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Knowledge (Nature)	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Nature)|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:An anima manipulates the very elements around himself. Path Sphere: Nature or Weather Path Possession: The anima may actively possess natural elements, creating a small elemental or animated plant. The creature dissipates when the possession ends. The created creature counts as willing. There must be a suitable volume of appropriate material. The anima may use talents such as Create Nature, or the Create Fire geomancing ability of the [fire] package as part of activating this ability to supply the required material, paying the normal cost for doing so. The available forms depend on the spheres and packages possessed. Air elementals require the [air] package or the Weather sphere and a given number of 5-foot cubes of air. Earth elementals require the [earth] or [metal] package and a given number of 5-foot cubes of stone, dirt, metal, or sand. Fire elementals require the [fire] package and Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Anima - Weather	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Weather Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_WEATHER|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Knowledge (Nature)	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Nature)|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:An anima manipulates the very elements around himself. Path Sphere: Nature or Weather Path Possession: The anima may actively possess natural elements, creating a small elemental or animated plant. The creature dissipates when the possession ends. The created creature counts as willing. There must be a suitable volume of appropriate material. The anima may use talents such as Create Nature, or the Create Fire geomancing ability of the [fire] package as part of activating this ability to supply the required material, paying the normal cost for doing so. The available forms depend on the spheres and packages possessed. Air elementals require the [air] package or the Weather sphere and a given number of 5-foot cubes of air. Earth elementals require the [earth] or [metal] package and a given number of 5-foot cubes of stone, dirt, metal, or sand. Fire elementals require the [fire] package and Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Corruptor	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Death Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_DEATH|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Knowledge (Religion)	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Religion)|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:A corruptor marshals an undead army to spread his influence. Path Sphere: Death Path Possession: The corruptor may actively possess dead bodies. The possessed creature has statistics as if it had been animated per the reanimate ability of the Death sphere, including any talents of that sphere that he possesses, and must meet all requirements of that ability. The target creature may have Hit Dice up to twice the corruptor’s class level. This stacks with Death caster levels gained from other sources. The created creature counts as willing. When the possession ends, the reanimate effect also ends. The possessed body does not count against the number of Hit Dice of undead the wraith can control. Path Skill: Knowledge [religion] [Int]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Cryptid	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Alteration Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_ALTERATION|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Handle Animal	BONUS:SKILL|Handle Animal|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Able to unlock the primal wrath of wild beasts, cryptids can be fearsome warriors. Path Sphere: Alteration Path Possession: Creatures of the animal type that are no worse than indifferent to the cryptid are counted as willing targets for possession. Creatures of the animal or magical beast types take a -2 penalty on saves against the cryptids possession. Path Skill: Handle Animal [Cha]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Despoiler	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Death Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_DEATH|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Heal	BONUS:SKILL|Heal|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:A despoiler feeds on pestilence and decay. Path Sphere: Death Path Possession: The despoiler may possess any creature of the vermin type, ignoring any type-based immunity to mind-affecting effects. Creatures suffering from the effects of poison or disease take a -2 penalty on saves against the despoiler’s possession. Path Skill: Heal [Wis]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Gremlin	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Technomancy Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_TECHNOMANCY|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Disable Device	BONUS:SKILL|Disable Device|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Source: Arcforge Players Compendium A gremlin interferes with technology and machinery, often by seizing direct control. Path Sphere: Technomancy Path Possession: The gremlin may actively possess unattended objects, animating them to serve. These objects count as being willing. The object must be of a size the wraith could animate per the Animate Object talent of the Enhancement sphere, using his class level as his caster level. This stacks normally with caster levels gained from other sources. The object gains the statistics and abilities as an animated object per the Animate Object talent of the Enhancement sphere. Path Skill: Disable Device [Dex]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Moroi	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Blood Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_BLOOD|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Heal	BONUS:SKILL|Heal|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Wraith that are drawn to, and sometimes feed on, blood. Path Sphere: Blood Path Possession: The moroi’s possession ability is treated as blood control for the purpose of determining save penalties from being less than half hit points. Path Skill: Heal [Wis]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Phantasm	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Illusion Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_ILLUSION|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Disguise	BONUS:SKILL|Disguise|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Hunters that hide inside their illusion, deceiving their prey into a false security. Path Sphere: Illusion Path Possession: Creatures within the area of an illusion created by the phantasm take a -2 penalty on saves against the phantasm’s possession. Path Skill: Disguise [Cha]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Poltergeist	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_TELEKINESIS|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Fly	BONUS:SKILL|Fly|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:A poltergeist is adept at moving creatures and objects as well as possessing and animating objects. Path Sphere: Telekinesis Path Possession: The poltergeist may actively possess unattended objects, animating them to serve. These objects count as being willing. The object must be of a size the wraith could animate per the Animate Objects talent of the Enhancement sphere, using his class level as his caster level. This stacks normally with caster levels gained from other sources. The object gains the statistics and abilities as an animated object per the Animate Object talent of the Enhancement sphere. Path Skill: Fly [Dex]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Presence	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Divination Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_DIVINATION|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Perception	BONUS:SKILL|Perception|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Source: Diamond Spheres: Erudition & Esoterica Known to reveal secrets and lost knowledge, a presence attempts to reveal what is lost. Path Sphere: Divination Path Possession: Creatures the presence is passively possessing may use the presence's bonus to Perception and Sense Motive instead of their own. Path Skill: Perception [Wis]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Revenant	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|War Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_WAR|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Intimidate	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Source: Diamond Spheres: Erudition & Esoterica Angry and consumed, revenants are hateful spirits that are fuelled by death and revenge. Path Sphere: War Path Possession: Creatures within the area of a totem created by the revenant take a -2 penalty on saves against the revenant's possession. Path Skill: Intimidate [Cha]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Shadow	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Dark Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_DARK|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Stealth	BONUS:SKILL|Stealth|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:A shadow lurks in darkness, seizing those foolish enough to enter their penumbra. Path Sphere: Dark Path Possession: Creatures within the area of a darkness created by the shadow take a -2 penalty on saves against the shadow’s possession. Path Skill: Stealth [Dex]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Soul	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Life Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_LIFE|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Heal	BONUS:SKILL|Heal|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Source: Diamond Spheres: Erudition & Esoterica The soul heals and repairs the spirit of those they influence. Path Sphere: Life Path Possession: Creatures the soul is passively possessing gain the benefits of his invigorate Life sphere ability for as long as he is possessing a creature. The soul must pay any costs associated with invigorate, if any. The temporary hit points granted by invigorate are replenished every round the creature is possessed. The effects of invigorate are lost when the possession ends. Path Skill: Heal [Wis]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Spook	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Mind Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_MIND|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Intimidate	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:A spook feeds on fear and insanity. Path Sphere: Mind Path Possession: Creatures the spook is passively possessing take a -2 penalty on saves against the spook’s charm abilities of the Mind sphere. Creatures that are cowering, panicked, or paralyzed take an additional -2 penalty on saves against the spook’s possession ability. Path Skill: Intimidate [Cha]  Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
Wraith Path of the Wisp	CATEGORY:Wraith Haunt Path	PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,1	ABILITY:Spheres Magic Talent|AUTOMATIC|Light Sphere	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_CL_LIGHT|SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL-floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL*3/4)	CSKILL:Knowledge (Nature)	BONUS:SKILL|Knowledge (Nature)|floor(SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL/2)|TYPE=Insight|PREVARGTEQ:SPHERES_WRAITH_LEVEL,4	DESC:Source: Diamond Spheres: Erudition & Esoterica Bringers of pale light and hope, wisps lead the way and guide the lost. Path Sphere: Light Path Possession: Whenever the wisp possesses a creature, he may immediately cause the creature to glow, as the Light sphere ability. Additionally, the wisp can possess a light source, as long as it is being produced by an unattended object. Light sources count as willing. The object must be of a size the wraith could animate [per the Animate Object Enhancement sphere talent], using his class level as his caster level—this stacks normally with caster levels gained from other sources. This does not grant control over the object itself, just the light source. If the wisp actively possesses a light source, he can change the light level and area as a free action, within the same limitations as his glow ability. If the wisp possesses a [nimbus] talent, he ca Consult source for unrepresented possession effects and duplicate-sphere replacement.
